{"text": "Grand River Counselling Collective\n22 Frederick Street, Suite 6, Kitchener ON  N2H 6M6\n\nPROGRESS NOTE -- INDIVIDUAL PSYCHOTHERAPY                      Session 7 of 12 (EAP)\n\nClient:      Ravinder Bhullar (\"Ravi\")         Chart: GRC-2026-0412\nDOB:         1994-04-18                       Health card: 4532 281 947 KM\nDate:        Tuesday, 6 October 2026, 5:00-5:50 pm, in person\nTherapist:   Catriona MacAskill, RP (CRPO # 009417)\nFunder:      Laurentide Benefit Assurance, EAP file LBA-EAP-771820; fee $165.00 billed direct\n\nPRESENTATION\nR.B. arrived on time, tired, tearful once. PHQ-9 = 14 (was 17 at intake), GAD-7 = 11.\nSleep 5 hrs. Reports two panic attacks at work since last session, both on the shop floor\nat Conestoga Precision Tooling, where he is the only apprentice on the night shift.\n\nRISK\nPassive suicidal ideation (\"wouldn't mind not waking up\") twice this week, no plan, no\nintent, no access to means. Safety plan reviewed. Protective: partner, his sister Harpreet.\n\nCONTENT\n- Came out to his parents as gay on Thanksgiving weekend. Father has not spoken to him\n  since. Family is observant Sikh; Ravi says the gurdwara community \"will know by now\".\n- Partner Devon Fairweather wants him to move in. R.B. fears this \"makes it final\" with his family.\n  Devon has offered to attend a session.\n- Cannabis nightly to sleep, up from weekends only. Drinking unchanged (2-3/week).\n- Started sertraline 50 mg via family doctor on Sept 21; nausea settling.\n- Worried the plant will find out: his supervisor signs the EAP attendance slips. Explained\n  that the slip shows dates only.\n\nINTERVENTION: CBT thought record on \"I have destroyed my family\"; grounding for panic;\nbehavioural activation (gym 2x). Psychoeducation re cannabis and sleep.\n\nASSESSMENT: Major depressive episode, moderate (DSM-5), with panic attacks. Improving\nslowly; acute stressor.\n\nPLAN\n1. Next session 13 Oct, 5 pm. Ask funder for 6 more sessions.\n2. With consent, short letter to family doctor re SI and medication.\n3. Emergency contact on file: Harpreet Bhullar, 519-555-0114. Client's cell 226 555 0172;\n   OK to leave voicemail, NOT ok to email his work address. Personal: rav.b94@inbox.example.\n\nSigned electronically: C. MacAskill, RP    2026-10-06 18:22", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "338 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ravinder Bhullar", "Catriona MacAskill", "Devon Fairweather", "Harpreet Bhullar", "family doctor"], "companies": ["Grand River Counselling Collective", "Conestoga Precision Tooling", "Laurentide Benefit Assurance", "Sikh", "gurdwara"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Kitchener", "Conestoga Precision Tooling", "Gurdwara community"], "health": ["panic attacks", "sleep 5 hrs", "PHQ-9 = 14", "GAD-7 = 11", "sertraline 50 mg", "cannabis nightly", "drinking 2-3/week", "psychological distress"], "sensitive": ["race or ethnicity", "religion", "political views or donations", "criminal history", "sexuality", "family dynamics"], "names": ["Ravinder", "Ravi", "Devon", "Harpreet"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 34, "text": "Grand River Counselling Collective", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Grand River Counselling Collective"}, {"start": 35, "end": 63, "text": "22 Frederick Street, Suite 6", "kind": "street", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "22 Frederick Street, Suite 6"}, {"start": 65, "end": 74, "text": "Kitchener", "kind": "places", "source": "model", "canonical": "Kitchener"}, {"start":